  "causal_findings": [
    "The same official certificate-B generator on full matched21-module/21-root contexts reproduces both exact historical recorded-source lengths at unchanged4194304 generation budget; no Bproof was reconstructed.",
    "The16-helper change adds16 actual target functions and16 FunOK theorem rows, while literal bytes, constructor/shape count, match-pair count and record-slot pressure stay unchanged. Helper calls are function references, not source/Rust inlining.",
    "The certificate encodes both the target program and closed Rust AST, plus explicit correspondence derivations with types, patterns and SSA contexts. Record field projections use full-arity patterns; this can grow quadratically with record width/depth.",
    "Global DAG hash-consing and printer sharing exist. Thus raw AST/node counts do not predict recorded-source bytes, and inclusive per-row reach counts overlap; do not sum them as exact file attribution.",
    "Both DAG12-byte lower bounds remain under4MiB, while actual canonical notation is6.7/6.86MiB. The normal final measured source-size guard refuses before returning/staging B; the absent failedBfile is expected.",
    "No source function names singletonBytes/RuntimeByteBuilder/clearCleanupTarget occur in either B record: this is not repeated raw source-name or source-text embedding.",
    "Actual byte attribution to program/krate/new helper proofs versus unchanged proof rows requires original-notation/DAG-sharing-aware row analysis. No claim is made that unchanged record_slots explains the162593-byte delta."
  ],
